     <article class="story single" data-beat="health">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">HEALTH</span> · ET Healthworld · 2026-10-21 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>GLP-1 Drugs Hailed as Breakthrough with Millions of Users, Projected Growth</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#GLP-1</span> <span>#Weight-loss drugs</span> <span>#Ozempic</span> <span>#Wegovy</span></div>
       <p>GLP-1 drugs, including Novo Nordisk's Ozempic and Wegovy, are being recognized as significant medical breakthroughs. These medications have demonstrated high efficacy in treating conditions such as obesity and type 2 diabetes, alongside reducing the risk of heart disease.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-21/glp-1-drugs-hailed-as-breakthrough-with-millions-of-users-pr.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Their impact is already widespread, with approximately 10 million Americans having used these drugs last year. Projections from JPMorgan research anticipate a substantial increase, estimating that usage could expand to 25 million by the year 2030.</p><p>This rapid adoption and projected growth underscore the transformative potential of GLP-1 drugs in public health, particularly in managing chronic conditions that affect millions globally.</p><p>What to watch: Continued research and market expansion of GLP-1 drugs.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately captures all concrete facts and figures provided in the source summary without padding.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://health.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/as-weight-loss-drug-users-turn-to-dietary-supplements-doctors-regulators-raise-flags/135085107" rel="noopener">ET Healthworld</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
