       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-21 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Madhvacharya Birth Anniversary Celebrated in Yadgir with Calls to Uphold Moral Values</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The birth anniversary of Jagadguru Srimad Madhvacharya, the exponent of Dvaita philosophy, was celebrated in Yadgir on Wednesday at an event organized by the district administration and Zilla Panchayat. Speakers at the Deputy Commissioner's office highlighted the saint-philosopher's contributions to religious, spiritual, and philosophical fields, stating his teachings continue to guide society and inspire moral values. Pandit Narasimhachar Puranik delivered a discourse urging people to incorporate Madhvacharya's principles into daily life.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-21/madhvacharya-birth-anniversary-celebrated-in-yadgir-with-cal.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Additional Deputy Commissioner Ramesh Kolar emphasized that observing the anniversaries of great philosophers helps spread their message among the public, and greeted members of the Vipra community. Prominent community members and local officials, including District Brahmin Association general secretary Shankar Narayan and advocate Narsingrao Kinikeri, offered floral tributes.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Faithful to the source event, speakers, and details of the celebration.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/karnataka/madhvacharyas-teachings-inspire-people-to-uphold-moral-values/article71607824.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
