     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-21 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Officials in Eluru, Krishna, and West Godavari Districts Observe Police Commemoration Day</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Police and Revenue department officials gathered across Eluru, Krishna, and West Godavari districts to pay floral tributes and recall the sacrifices of police martyrs on Police Commemoration Day. Eluru Range IGP G.V.G. Ashok Kumar, Collector K. Vetriselvi, and SP K. Pratap Shiva Kishore presented mementos to families of slain officers in Eluru. Officials announced instructions to relieve officers suffering from chronic diseases from bandobust duties and conduct regular medical check-ups.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-21/officials-in-eluru-krishna-and-west-godavari-districts-obser.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In Krishna district, Collector D.K. Balaji and SP V. Vidyasagar Naidu paid tributes at the Martyrs Pylon in Machilipatnam, urging officers to work with dedication. In West Godavari, SP Adnan Nayeem Asmi noted that 154 police personnel died on duty nationwide last year during the district commemoration event near Bhimavaram.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: All main figures, tributes, and announcements across the three districts are accurately captured.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/police-commemoration-days-officials-of-eluru-krishna-west-godavari-districts-pay-tributes-to-martyrs/article71608144.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
