     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-21 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Shooters targeted Bollywood actors before Tiger Shroff</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Mumbai Crime Branch officials revealed that the three suspects arrested in the Tiger Shroff firing incident had originally surveyed three other prominent Bollywood actors. The accused abandoned plans to target these individuals due to stringent security measures at their residences.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-21/shooters-targeted-bollywood-actors-before-tiger-shroff.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Following these failed attempts, the suspects allegedly shifted their focus to Shroff, viewing him as an easier target. The three accused, including individuals from Bihar and Haryana, were apprehended on a train in Kota and subsequently brought to Mumbai for interrogation. The firing occurred in Juhu on Sunday, leaving the actor unharmed while his driver sustained injuries.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately captures the essence of the report without unnecessary fluff.</p>
