       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · BBC Business · 2026-10-21 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Solicitor investigated for advising on illegal worker fine evasion</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#business</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A Bradford-based solicitor, Mohammad Alias Yousaf, was secretly filmed by the BBC advising an undercover reporter on how to avoid a £45,000 fine for employing an illegal worker. The solicitor allegedly suggested that the client could evade the penalty by finding a person overseas to falsely claim ownership of the business.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-21/solicitor-investigated-for-advising-on-illegal-worker-fine-e.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Yousaf has denied providing this advice or submitting false information to the Home Office. In response to the investigation, Home Secretary Shabana Mahmood announced a formal review of the processes used to issue and collect fines for illegal employment.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate, neutral reporting of the allegations and the official response.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
