     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-21 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Two women arrested in Mumbai shooting case as families struggle with migrant worker backgrounds</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Delhi Police Special Cell arrested two young women, Radha from Sitapur and Babita from Azamgarh, regarding an October 18 firing incident involving Bollywood actor Tiger Shroff. Police allege the women transported a bag containing a pistol and ammunition from Delhi to Mumbai. Relatives in their home villages described the suspects as migrant workers who left home seeking regular wages and independence.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-21/two-women-arrested-in-mumbai-shooting-case-as-families-strug.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Babita's family stated she moved to Sonipat, Haryana, roughly two years ago for packaging work paying between Rs 10,000 and Rs 12,000 a month. Her sister Neelam noted Babita was a graduate who could not find stable local work. Relatives expressed distress, stating Babita had no prior criminal record and they are relying on news reports to understand the allegations.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately summarises the migrant background and arrests, minor background details omitted due to brevity.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/india/from-ups-villages-to-mumbais-gunfire-untold-stories-of-2-women-accused-in-tiger-shroff-shooting-case-ws-blrt-10391848.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/mumbai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mumbai</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
